a9431581e9a1b0278a977a64c0d727c73d.png)\n\nThe function is not defined for $x\\le -2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{-}}{log}_{2}⁡(x+2)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is defined for $x>-2.$ Moreover,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -{2}^{+}}{log}_{2}⁡(x+2)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are not equal, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -2}{log}_{2}⁡(x+2)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564521 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105724 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "f956a45f-29cb-5b78-a29f-3796e22af09d" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Limits at Infinity of Logarithmic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4311460d-7209-5e54-a0b7-67b51a9bc81d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564082} {:answer/id #uuid "568e7cb8-4ae6-57c4-bce6-a2ae6bbb1708" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564107} {:answer/id #uuid "88037992-96b5-5395-8932-76ce51e1d6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564179} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ffc733-c712-56a3-aa30-c093fb44a64e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564285} {:answer/id #uuid "d95a6df9-7b43-5091-bfef-202f1b31f8a2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564311}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "88037992-96b5-5395-8932-76ce51e1d6dc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564179} :answer-field/id #uuid "21f64035-7ada-5e92-aa3a-3415a6fccd66" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564384}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c386627f-74f0-5d5a-9a11-2fd0a0613fa9" :question/math-academy-id "q-78092" :question/problem "${lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{log}_{5}⁡(x+1)=$" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the graph of $y=\\operatorname{log}⁡(x+1).$\n\n![](images/90/902c8394181aefb301c901b3792e89e909ba36ecba3a9b8113fc42b80fd08870.png)\n\nFrom the graph, we see that the function increases without bound as $x$ increases. Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to \\infty }{log}_{5}⁡(x+1)=\\infty \n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186564478 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186105725 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bae52078-17b6-536d-9cf8-4a92b811c2ae" :knowledge-point/title "Evaluating Infinite Limits of Logarithmic Functions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cba6f4f-7f15-556c-a7f3-40384f4762be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563990} {:answer/id #uuid "13b7b802-4cfb-59ae-8f7e-a0a096cb02e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186563996} {:answer/id #uuid "6532bdbf-67c3-5cb8-b17b-f39dc8c37c15" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564129} {:answer/id #uuid "77699979-865d-5845-a4a5-998145367451" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\infty " :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564150} {:answer/id #uuid "cf45625d-0eac-56fb-9026-80a2e5480905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cf45625d-0eac-56fb-9026-80a2e5480905" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{DNE}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564295} :answer-field/id #uuid "ef353a81-f085-5f7c-bea2-edd66e33a6a2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186564456}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "29481c76-b7fa-575a-9ace-40d060b32844" :question/math-academy-id "q-78102" :question/problem "Calculate ${lim}_{x\\to -3}{log}_{7}⁡(x+3).$" :question/worked-solution "Let's sketch the graph of $y={log}_{7}⁡(x+3).$\n\n![](images/0b/0b45cd648830ad88c2f21865c1bfd704783a7b5d9ce3510646ae55e98d2d95ac.png)\n\nThe function is not defined for $x\\le -3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{-}}{log}_{7}⁡(x+3)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$\n\nHowever, the function is defined for $x>-3.$ Moreover,\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to (-3)^{+}}{log}_{7}⁡(x+3)=-\\infty .\n$$\n\nSince the left and right-sided limits are not equal, we have\n\n$$\n{lim}_{x\\to -3}{log}_{7}⁡(x+3)=\\text{DNE}.\n$$"}]}
